      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-q/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) Substituting P = (0, 8) gives 24 sin θ = 12, [M1] so θ = π/6 or 5π/6. [A1] The two tangent equations √ are 3 2y + 2 3x = 12 and √ 3 2y −2 3x = 12. [M1] [A1] √ √ √ √ At Q, set y = 0, giving 2 3x = 12 or −2 3x = 12, hence x = ±6/ 3, or x = ±2 3. [A1] In either √ case the perpendicular base and height are 8 and 2 3. [A1] The triangle has area √ √ 1 2(8)(2 3) = 8 3 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 12 is 12 marks.</p>"
